# closure_in_generic_body - a closure written in a generic body is generic over the body's type parameters, so it may capture values of them (owned by a `move` closure and released once, or borrowed), take and return them, be called where it is made or passed to a callable-bounded parameter, and be written in a method of a generic owner; each copy of the body has its own closure.
